window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b224-be872ef985b2c071.json"]={sha256:"be872ef985b2c0713ad3ea40fb2b689adce6fa64a74f2ea44bc7d771f0a7b862",value:{"id":"b224","title":"威尼斯 MOSE 防潮系統","titleEn":"Venice MOSE flood barriers","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課以威尼斯 MOSE 防潮系統為入口，深入浮動翻板、壓縮空氣與潟湖環境的耦合。十個單元各自對應不同的荷載路徑、能量交換或監測問題，從守恆式建立量化估算，再檢查量測配置是否能辨認真正失效原因。工程史實只採用列明範圍的公開一手資料；所有模型輸入另標為教學假設，成果是可追溯的工程判讀紀錄。","summaryEn":"Using Venice MOSE flood barriers as its entry point, this course examines coupling buoyant flap gates, compressed air and lagoon environmental response. Ten units address different load paths, energy exchanges or monitoring questions, starting with conservation-based estimates and testing whether observations distinguish failure causes. Historical statements use scoped primary evidence. Numerical model inputs are separately identified as teaching assumptions, producing a traceable engineering interpretation record.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-systems","subcategoryTitle":"防潮、航運與大壩施工","subcategoryTitleEn":"Tidal barriers, navigation and dam construction","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-systems","learningTags":["water","water-systems","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-gate","architectureNodes":[["浮力翻轉與重心","Buoyant rotation and centroids"],["空氣供應與壓縮功","Air supply and compression work"],["波浪激振與自振","Wave excitation and natural period"],["關閉潟湖降雨收支","Rainfall balance in an isolated lagoon"],["供氣網路可用度","Air-network availability"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"water-gate","labels":["浮力翻轉與重心","空氣供應與壓縮功","波浪激振與自振","關閉潟湖降雨收支","供氣網路可用度"],"labelsEn":["Buoyant rotation and centroids","Air supply and compression work","Wave excitation and natural period","Rainfall balance in an isolated lagoon","Air-network availability"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"本課原創比較練習分兩個相互獨立的物理模型。教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設有效排水體積500 m³、海水密度1025 kg/m³、浮力臂3 m，自重3 MN、重心臂4 m；淨復原矩為3.083 MN·m，限靜水姿態。教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設海水深8 m、密度1025 kg/m³、大氣壓101.3 kPa，靜水表壓80.442 kPa、絕壓181.742 kPa；不含管損與動態壓差。先逐一圈出公式內的控制體、力方向或時間尺度，再把每項輸入的量綱換成一致單位。第二人只根據輸入重算結果，不抄第一人的中間數字。最後指出這兩個估算尚未包含的空間變化、非線性及量測誤差；若將結果用於另一座工程，必須重建其幾何、材料與邊界條件，不能挪用本練習的假設。 靜水壓敏感度固定ρ=1025 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²及大氣壓101.3 kPa，只將水深8 m增為10 m。表壓ρgh由80.442增至100.5525 kPa，增加25%；絕壓則由181.742增至201.8525 kPa，其增幅不是25%。比較只包含靜水柱，不推定送氣管損、閘門浮力或動態壓力同步變化。","textEn":"This original comparison exercise uses two independent physical models. Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume displaced volume 500 m³, seawater density 1025 kg/m³, buoyancy arm 3 m, weight 3 MN and weight arm 4 m. Net restoring moment is 3.083 MN·m for that hydrostatic posture. Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume seawater depth 8 m, density 1025 kg/m³ and atmospheric pressure 101.3 kPa. Gauge pressure is 80.442 kPa and absolute pressure 181.742 kPa, excluding piping losses and dynamics. First identify the control volume, force direction or time scale in each relation, then convert every input to consistent units. A second reviewer recalculates from the inputs without copying intermediate numbers. Finally identify spatial variability, nonlinear effects and measurement errors omitted by both estimates. Transfer to another structure requires rebuilding its geometry, material description and boundary conditions; the assumed classroom inputs are not transferable design or operating parameters. For hydrostatic sensitivity, hold ρ=1025 kg/m³, g=9.81 m/s² and atmospheric pressure 101.3 kPa fixed, increasing only depth from 8 m to 10 m. Gauge pressure ρgh rises from 80.442 to 100.5525 kPa, or 25%; absolute pressure rises from 181.742 to 201.8525 kPa, not by 25%. This column calculation does not infer pipe losses, gate buoyancy or dynamic pressures.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b224-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「浮力翻轉與重心」與「氣壓水深與絕對壓力」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Buoyant rotation and centroids\" and \"Air pressure and absolute pressure\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b224-v15-01","title":"浮力翻轉與重心：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Buoyant rotation and centroids: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「浮力翻轉與重心」如何影響威尼斯 MOSE 防潮系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Buoyant rotation and centroids” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Venice MOSE flood barriers”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"翻板內水被空氣置換後，浮力和自重對鉸軸的力矩改變，門體才會轉動。上浮不是氣壓直接把整片門推出水面，還必須考慮外部水壓和重心位置。 取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設有效排水體積500 m³、海水密度1025 kg/m³、浮力臂3 m，自重3 MN、重心臂4 m；淨復原矩為3.083 MN·m，限靜水姿態。 氣室進水不均會移動重心，改變各鉸座受力。若把完全浸沒的浮力公式沿用到出水後，排水體積與力臂都會錯，進而誤判平衡角度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「浮力翻轉與重心」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Replacing internal water with air changes buoyancy and weight moments about the hinge. Rotation is not simply air pressure pushing the entire gate upward; external pressure and centroid positions also matter. Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume displaced volume 500 m³, seawater density 1025 kg/m³, buoyancy arm 3 m, weight 3 MN and weight arm 4 m. Net restoring moment is 3.083 MN·m for that hydrostatic posture. Unequal flooding shifts the center of gravity and hinge reactions. Reusing fully submerged buoyancy after emergence gives incorrect displacement and lever arms, leading to a false equilibrium angle. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Buoyant rotation and centroids” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s².","failure":"常見誤解：「總浮力大於自重就能直接決定翻板的唯一平衡角。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Buoyancy exceeding weight directly determines the unique flap equilibrium angle.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「浮力翻轉與重心」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Buoyant rotation and centroids”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b224-v15-01-k1","title":"浮力翻轉與重心","titleEn":"Buoyant rotation and centroids","text":"翻板內水被空氣置換後，浮力和自重對鉸軸的力矩改變，門體才會轉動。上浮不是氣壓直接把整片門推出水面，還必須考慮外部水壓和重心位置。","textEn":"Replacing internal water with air changes buoyancy and weight moments about the hinge. Rotation is not simply air pressure pushing the entire gate upward; external pressure and centroid positions also matter.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b224-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：總浮力大於自重就能直接決定翻板的唯一平衡角。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Buoyancy exceeding weight directly determines the unique flap equilibrium angle. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「浮力翻轉與重心」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Buoyant rotation and centroids\" is correct?","options":["總浮力大於自重就能直接決定翻板的唯一平衡角。","翻板內水被空氣置換後，浮力和自重對鉸軸的力矩改變，門體才會轉動。","氣體狀態換算可以直接用表壓取代絕對壓力。"],"optionsEn":["Buoyancy exceeding weight directly determines the unique flap equilibrium angle.","Replacing internal water with air changes buoyancy and weight moments about the hinge.","Gas-state calculations can directly substitute gauge pressure for absolute pressure."],"answer":1,"explanation":"翻板內水被空氣置換後，浮力和自重對鉸軸的力矩改變，門體才會轉動。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Replacing internal water with air changes buoyancy and weight moments about the hinge. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b224-v15-02","title":"浮力翻轉與重心：定量估算","titleEn":"Buoyant rotation and centroids: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b224-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「浮力翻轉與重心」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Buoyant rotation and centroids” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設有效排水體積500 m³、海水密度1025 kg/m³、浮力臂3 m，自重3 MN、重心臂4 m；淨復原矩為3.083 MN·m，限靜水姿態。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume displaced volume 500 m³, seawater density 1025 kg/m³, buoyancy arm 3 m, weight 3 MN and weight arm 4 m. Net restoring moment is 3.083 MN·m for that hydrostatic posture. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以門角、內外水位與艙氣壓同步重建排水體積，將浮心與重心分開定位；檢查力矩符號是否隨角度改變，避免只比較總浮力與重量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Reconstruct displacement from synchronized angle, internal and external levels and air pressure.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b224-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設有效排水體積500 m³、海水密度1025 kg/m³、浮力臂3 m，自重3 MN、重心臂4 m；淨復原矩為3.083 MN·m，限靜水姿態。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume displaced volume 500 m³, seawater density 1025 kg/m³, buoyancy arm 3 m, weight 3 MN and weight arm 4 m. Net restoring moment is 3.083 MN·m for that hydrostatic posture.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b224-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「浮力翻轉與重心」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Buoyant rotation and centroids\", which statement holds?","options":["只要有兩座鉸鏈，每座就永遠承受一半荷載。","兩片門振幅相同就表示它們沒有相對運動。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。"],"optionsEn":["With two hinges each always carries exactly half the applied load.","Two gates with equal amplitudes have no relative motion between them.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s²."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b224-v15-03","title":"浮力翻轉與重心：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Buoyant rotation and centroids: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b224-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「浮力翻轉與重心」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Buoyant rotation and centroids” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以門角、內外水位與艙氣壓同步重建排水體積，將浮心與重心分開定位；檢查力矩符號是否隨角度改變，避免只比較總浮力與重量。逐角度積分濕潤體積與浮心位置，確認門體開始露出水面後仍使用正確幾何。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Reconstruct displacement from synchronized angle, internal and external levels and air pressure. Locate buoyancy and gravity centroids separately and check moment signs as angle changes instead of comparing forces alone. Integrate wetted volume and buoyancy centroid at each angle, checking geometry after the gate begins emerging above water. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以浮力翻轉與重心編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。以門角、內外水位與艙氣壓同步重建排水體積，將浮心與重心分開定位；檢查力矩符號是否隨角度改變，避免只比較總浮力與重量。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for buoyant rotation and centroids, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Reconstruct displacement from synchronized angle, internal and external levels and air pressure. Locate buoyancy and gravity centroids separately and check moment signs as angle changes instead of comparing forces alone.","failure":"注意干擾：氣室進水不均會移動重心，改變各鉸座受力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Unequal flooding shifts the center of gravity and hinge reactions. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b224-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以門角、內外水位與艙氣壓同步重建排水體積，將浮心與重心分開定位；檢查力矩符號是否隨角度改變，避免只比較總浮力與重量。逐角度積分濕潤體積與浮心位置，確認門體開始露出水面後仍使用正確幾何。","textEn":"Reconstruct displacement from synchronized angle, internal and external levels and air pressure. Locate buoyancy and gravity centroids separately and check moment signs as angle changes instead of comparing forces alone. Integrate wetted volume and buoyancy centroid at each angle, checking geometry after the gate begins emerging above water.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b224-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以浮力翻轉與重心編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。以門角、內外水位與艙氣壓同步重建排水體積，將浮心與重心分開定位；檢查力矩符號是否隨角度改變，避免只比較總浮力與重量。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for buoyant rotation and centroids, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Reconstruct displacement from synchronized angle, internal and external levels and air pressure. Locate buoyancy and gravity centroids separately and check moment signs as angle changes instead of comparing forces alone.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「浮力翻轉與重心」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Buoyant rotation and centroids\"?","options":["以門角、內外水位與艙氣壓同步重建排水體積，將浮心與重心分開定位；檢查力矩符號是否隨角度改變，避免只比較總浮力與重量。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","平均鹽度降低就證明底層高鹽水已完全排出。"],"optionsEn":["Reconstruct displacement from synchronized angle, internal and external levels and air pressure.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Lower mean salinity proves that all saline bottom water has been removed."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以門角、內外水位與艙氣壓同步重建排水體積，將浮心與重心分開定位；檢查力矩符號是否隨角度改變，避免只比較總浮力與重量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Reconstruct displacement from synchronized angle, internal and external levels and air pressure. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b224-v15-04","title":"浮力翻轉與重心：失效診斷","titleEn":"Buoyant rotation and centroids: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b224-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「浮力翻轉與重心」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Buoyant rotation and centroids” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"氣室進水不均會移動重心，改變各鉸座受力。若把完全浸沒的浮力公式沿用到出水後，排水體積與力臂都會錯，進而誤判平衡角度。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Unequal flooding shifts the center of gravity and hinge reactions. Reusing fully submerged buoyancy after emergence gives incorrect displacement and lever arms, leading to a false equilibrium angle. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：若把完全浸沒的浮力公式沿用到出水後，排水體積與力臂都會錯，進而誤判平衡角度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Reusing fully submerged buoyancy after emergence gives incorrect displacement and lever arms, leading to a false equilibrium angle.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「總浮力大於自重就能直接決定翻板的唯一平衡角。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Buoyancy exceeding weight directly determines the unique flap equilibrium angle.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b224-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"氣室進水不均會移動重心，改變各鉸座受力。若把完全浸沒的浮力公式沿用到出水後，排水體積與力臂都會錯，進而誤判平衡角度。","textEn":"Unequal flooding shifts the center of gravity and hinge reactions. Reusing fully submerged buoyancy after emergence gives incorrect displacement and lever arms, leading to a false equilibrium angle.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b224-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「浮力翻轉與重心」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Buoyant rotation and centroids\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","氣室進水不均會移動重心，改變各鉸座受力。","氣體狀態換算可以直接用表壓取代絕對壓力。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Unequal flooding shifts the center of gravity and hinge reactions.","Gas-state calculations can directly substitute gauge pressure for absolute pressure."],"answer":1,"explanation":"氣室進水不均會移動重心，改變各鉸座受力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Unequal flooding shifts the center of gravity and hinge reactions. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b224-v15-05","title":"氣壓水深與絕對壓力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Air pressure and absolute pressure: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b224-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「氣壓水深與絕對壓力」如何影響威尼斯 MOSE 防潮系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Air pressure and absolute pressure” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Venice MOSE flood barriers”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"排水用空氣必須克服水深造成的外壓，壓縮氣體的狀態方程則使用絕對壓力。把表壓帶入氣體體積換算，會造成系統性的質量估算錯誤。 取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設海水深8 m、密度1025 kg/m³、大氣壓101.3 kPa，靜水表壓80.442 kPa、絕壓181.742 kPa；不含管損與動態壓差。 導壓管積水會改變零點，溫度變動也會使封閉氣體壓力改變。若只用壓力上升判斷門位，可能把管路堵塞或熱效應當成正常浮升。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「氣壓水深與絕對壓力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Displacement air must overcome external water pressure, while gas state relations require absolute pressure. Inserting gauge pressure into volume conversion systematically miscalculates air mass. Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume seawater depth 8 m, density 1025 kg/m³ and atmospheric pressure 101.3 kPa. Gauge pressure is 80.442 kPa and absolute pressure 181.742 kPa, excluding piping losses and dynamics. Water in impulse lines changes zero, and temperature changes pressure in confined air. Pressure rise alone can therefore mistake blockage or thermal effects for the expected gate movement. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Air pressure and absolute pressure” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s².","failure":"常見誤解：「氣體狀態換算可以直接用表壓取代絕對壓力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Gas-state calculations can directly substitute gauge pressure for absolute pressure.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「氣壓水深與絕對壓力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Air pressure and absolute pressure”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b224-v15-05-k1","title":"氣壓水深與絕對壓力","titleEn":"Air pressure and absolute pressure","text":"排水用空氣必須克服水深造成的外壓，壓縮氣體的狀態方程則使用絕對壓力。把表壓帶入氣體體積換算，會造成系統性的質量估算錯誤。","textEn":"Displacement air must overcome external water pressure, while gas state relations require absolute pressure. Inserting gauge pressure into volume conversion systematically miscalculates air mass.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b224-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：氣體狀態換算可以直接用表壓取代絕對壓力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Gas-state calculations can directly substitute gauge pressure for absolute pressure. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「氣壓水深與絕對壓力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Air pressure and absolute pressure\" is correct?","options":["氣體狀態換算可以直接用表壓取代絕對壓力。","供氣量增加一定等比例增加浮門的排水體積。","排水用空氣必須克服水深造成的外壓，壓縮氣體的狀態方程則使用絕對壓力。"],"optionsEn":["Gas-state calculations can directly substitute gauge pressure for absolute pressure.","Increasing supplied air always proportionally increases the gates displaced water volume.","Displacement air must overcome external water pressure, while gas state relations require absolute pressure."],"answer":2,"explanation":"排水用空氣必須克服水深造成的外壓，壓縮氣體的狀態方程則使用絕對壓力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Displacement air must overcome external water pressure, while gas state relations require absolute pressure. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b224-v15-06","title":"氣壓水深與絕對壓力：定量估算","titleEn":"Air pressure and absolute pressure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b224-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「氣壓水深與絕對壓力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Air pressure and absolute pressure” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設海水深8 m、密度1025 kg/m³、大氣壓101.3 kPa，靜水表壓80.442 kPa、絕壓181.742 kPa；不含管損與動態壓差。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume seawater depth 8 m, density 1025 kg/m³ and atmospheric pressure 101.3 kPa. Gauge pressure is 80.442 kPa and absolute pressure 181.742 kPa, excluding piping losses and dynamics. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：標明每支壓力計為表壓或絕壓，核對取壓點高程和當時大氣壓；利用獨立水位量測交叉檢查氣壓所推得的水柱高度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Identify each gauge as relative or absolute, checking tapping elevation and atmospheric pressure.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b224-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設海水深8 m、密度1025 kg/m³、大氣壓101.3 kPa，靜水表壓80.442 kPa、絕壓181.742 kPa；不含管損與動態壓差。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume seawater depth 8 m, density 1025 kg/m³ and atmospheric pressure 101.3 kPa. Gauge pressure is 80.442 kPa and absolute pressure 181.742 kPa, excluding piping losses and dynamics.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b224-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「氣壓水深與絕對壓力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Air pressure and absolute pressure\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。","浮門乾態自振週期可以直接當成水中的自振週期。","海口關閉後，潟湖內水量就必定保持固定。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s².","A dry gate natural period can directly represent its wet natural period.","Once the inlets close the lagoon water volume must remain constant."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b224-v15-07","title":"氣壓水深與絕對壓力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Air pressure and absolute pressure: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b224-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「氣壓水深與絕對壓力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Air pressure and absolute pressure” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"標明每支壓力計為表壓或絕壓，核對取壓點高程和當時大氣壓；利用獨立水位量測交叉檢查氣壓所推得的水柱高度。用靜止水柱核驗表壓轉換，檢查導壓管高差是否被正確加回水深推估。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Identify each gauge as relative or absolute, checking tapping elevation and atmospheric pressure. Cross-check the water-column height inferred from air pressure against independent level measurements. Verify gauge conversion with a stationary water column and check that impulse-line elevation is correctly included in depth inference. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以氣壓水深與絕對壓力編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。標明每支壓力計為表壓或絕壓，核對取壓點高程和當時大氣壓；利用獨立水位量測交叉檢查氣壓所推得的水柱高度。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for air pressure and absolute pressure, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Identify each gauge as relative or absolute, checking tapping elevation and atmospheric pressure. Cross-check the water-column height inferred from air pressure against independent level measurements.","failure":"注意干擾：導壓管積水會改變零點，溫度變動也會使封閉氣體壓力改變。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Water in impulse lines changes zero, and temperature changes pressure in confined air. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b224-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"標明每支壓力計為表壓或絕壓，核對取壓點高程和當時大氣壓；利用獨立水位量測交叉檢查氣壓所推得的水柱高度。用靜止水柱核驗表壓轉換，檢查導壓管高差是否被正確加回水深推估。","textEn":"Identify each gauge as relative or absolute, checking tapping elevation and atmospheric pressure. Cross-check the water-column height inferred from air pressure against independent level measurements. Verify gauge conversion with a stationary water column and check that impulse-line elevation is correctly included in depth inference.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b224-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以氣壓水深與絕對壓力編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。標明每支壓力計為表壓或絕壓，核對取壓點高程和當時大氣壓；利用獨立水位量測交叉檢查氣壓所推得的水柱高度。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for air pressure and absolute pressure, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Identify each gauge as relative or absolute, checking tapping elevation and atmospheric pressure. Cross-check the water-column height inferred from air pressure against independent level measurements.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「氣壓水深與絕對壓力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Air pressure and absolute pressure\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","標明每支壓力計為表壓或絕壓，核對取壓點高程和當時大氣壓；利用獨立水位量測交叉檢查氣壓所推得的水柱高度。","壓力感測器讀數一致就證明共同取壓管沒有問題。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Identify each gauge as relative or absolute, checking tapping elevation and atmospheric pressure.","Matching pressure readings prove the shared impulse connection has no defect."],"answer":1,"explanation":"標明每支壓力計為表壓或絕壓，核對取壓點高程和當時大氣壓；利用獨立水位量測交叉檢查氣壓所推得的水柱高度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Identify each gauge as relative or absolute, checking tapping elevation and atmospheric pressure. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b224-v15-08","title":"氣壓水深與絕對壓力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Air pressure and absolute pressure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b224-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「氣壓水深與絕對壓力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Air pressure and absolute pressure” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"導壓管積水會改變零點，溫度變動也會使封閉氣體壓力改變。若只用壓力上升判斷門位，可能把管路堵塞或熱效應當成正常浮升。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Water in impulse lines changes zero, and temperature changes pressure in confined air. Pressure rise alone can therefore mistake blockage or thermal effects for the expected gate movement. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：若只用壓力上升判斷門位，可能把管路堵塞或熱效應當成正常浮升。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Pressure rise alone can therefore mistake blockage or thermal effects for the expected gate movement.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「氣體狀態換算可以直接用表壓取代絕對壓力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Gas-state calculations can directly substitute gauge pressure for absolute pressure.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b224-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"導壓管積水會改變零點，溫度變動也會使封閉氣體壓力改變。若只用壓力上升判斷門位，可能把管路堵塞或熱效應當成正常浮升。","textEn":"Water in impulse lines changes zero, and temperature changes pressure in confined air. Pressure rise alone can therefore mistake blockage or thermal effects for the expected gate movement.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b224-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「氣壓水深與絕對壓力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Air pressure and absolute pressure\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","供氣量增加一定等比例增加浮門的排水體積。","導壓管積水會改變零點，溫度變動也會使封閉氣體壓力改變。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Increasing supplied air always proportionally increases the gates displaced water volume.","Water in impulse lines changes zero, and temperature changes pressure in confined air."],"answer":2,"explanation":"導壓管積水會改變零點，溫度變動也會使封閉氣體壓力改變。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Water in impulse lines changes zero, and temperature changes pressure in confined air. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b224-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「空氣供應與壓縮功」與「鉸座荷載分配」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Air supply and compression work\" and \"Hinge reaction distribution\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b224-v15-09","title":"空氣供應與壓縮功：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Air supply and compression work: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b224-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「空氣供應與壓縮功」如何影響威尼斯 MOSE 防潮系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Air supply and compression work” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Venice MOSE flood barriers”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"壓縮機功率取決於壓比、流量、熱交換和效率，注入體積不是同壓力下的自由空氣體積。理想等溫模型提供能耗下界，不能代表真實機組效率。 假設自由空氣流量2 m³/s、入口絕壓100 kPa、出口200 kPa，等溫理想功率p1Q1ln(p2/p1)=138.63 kW；未含機械與熱損失。 壓縮熱若未散去，等溫假設會低估功率；漏氣又使供氣量不等於有效排水量。把氣量和門體位移直接一對一換算，會漏掉可壓縮儲能。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「空氣供應與壓縮功」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Compressor power depends on pressure ratio, flow, heat exchange and efficiency. Delivered volume is not free-air volume at the same pressure. Ideal isothermal work is a lower-bound model, not an actual machine rating. Assume free-air flow 2 m³/s, inlet absolute pressure 100 kPa and outlet 200 kPa. Ideal isothermal power p1Q1ln(p2/p1)=138.63 kW, excluding mechanical and thermal losses. Incomplete heat rejection makes the isothermal estimate optimistic, and leakage separates supplied air from effective displacement. Equating air volume directly with gate movement ignores compressible energy stored in the system. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Air supply and compression work” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設自由空氣流量2 m³/s、入口絕壓100 kPa、出口200 kPa，等溫理想功率p1Q1ln(p2/p1)=138.63 kW；未含機械與熱損失。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume free-air flow 2 m³/s, inlet absolute pressure 100 kPa and outlet 200 kPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「供氣量增加一定等比例增加浮門的排水體積。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Increasing supplied air always proportionally increases the gates displaced water volume.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「空氣供應與壓縮功」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Air supply and compression work”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b224-v15-09-k1","title":"空氣供應與壓縮功","titleEn":"Air supply and compression work","text":"壓縮機功率取決於壓比、流量、熱交換和效率，注入體積不是同壓力下的自由空氣體積。理想等溫模型提供能耗下界，不能代表真實機組效率。","textEn":"Compressor power depends on pressure ratio, flow, heat exchange and efficiency. Delivered volume is not free-air volume at the same pressure.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b224-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：供氣量增加一定等比例增加浮門的排水體積。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Increasing supplied air always proportionally increases the gates displaced water volume. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「空氣供應與壓縮功」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Air supply and compression work\" is correct?","options":["壓縮機功率取決於壓比、流量、熱交換和效率，注入體積不是同壓力下的自由空氣體積。","供氣量增加一定等比例增加浮門的排水體積。","只要有兩座鉸鏈，每座就永遠承受一半荷載。"],"optionsEn":["Compressor power depends on pressure ratio, flow, heat exchange and efficiency.","Increasing supplied air always proportionally increases the gates displaced water volume.","With two hinges each always carries exactly half the applied load."],"answer":0,"explanation":"壓縮機功率取決於壓比、流量、熱交換和效率，注入體積不是同壓力下的自由空氣體積。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Compressor power depends on pressure ratio, flow, heat exchange and efficiency. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b224-v15-10","title":"空氣供應與壓縮功：定量估算","titleEn":"Air supply and compression work: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b224-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「空氣供應與壓縮功」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Air supply and compression work” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設自由空氣流量2 m³/s、入口絕壓100 kPa、出口200 kPa，等溫理想功率p1Q1ln(p2/p1)=138.63 kW；未含機械與熱損失。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume free-air flow 2 m³/s, inlet absolute pressure 100 kPa and outlet 200 kPa. Ideal isothermal power p1Q1ln(p2/p1)=138.63 kW, excluding mechanical and thermal losses. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：記錄流量換算的參考溫壓，對照壓縮機入口出口狀態和電功率；用儲氣壓力變化核對總氣量平衡，避免把瞬時充氣量當長期平均。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record flow reference temperature and pressure, comparing compressor inlet and outlet states with electrical power.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b224-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設自由空氣流量2 m³/s、入口絕壓100 kPa、出口200 kPa，等溫理想功率p1Q1ln(p2/p1)=138.63 kW；未含機械與熱損失。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume free-air flow 2 m³/s, inlet absolute pressure 100 kPa and outlet 200 kPa. Ideal isothermal power p1Q1ln(p2/p1)=138.63 kW, excluding mechanical and thermal losses.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b224-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「空氣供應與壓縮功」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Air supply and compression work\", which statement holds?","options":["兩片門振幅相同就表示它們沒有相對運動。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設自由空氣流量2 m³/s、入口絕壓100 kPa、出口200 kPa，等溫理想功率p1Q1ln(p2/p1)=138.63 kW。","平均鹽度降低就證明底層高鹽水已完全排出。"],"optionsEn":["Two gates with equal amplitudes have no relative motion between them.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume free-air flow 2 m³/s, inlet absolute pressure 100 kPa and outlet 200 kPa.","Lower mean salinity proves that all saline bottom water has been removed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設自由空氣流量2 m³/s、入口絕壓100 kPa、出口200 kPa，等溫理想功率p1Q1ln(p2/p1)=138.63 kW；未含機械與熱損失。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume free-air flow 2 m³/s, inlet absolute pressure 100 kPa and outlet 200 kPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b224-v15-11","title":"空氣供應與壓縮功：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Air supply and compression work: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b224-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「空氣供應與壓縮功」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Air supply and compression work” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"記錄流量換算的參考溫壓，對照壓縮機入口出口狀態和電功率；用儲氣壓力變化核對總氣量平衡，避免把瞬時充氣量當長期平均。用入口質量流率與儲氣質量增量閉合空氣平衡，另列溫升和漏氣造成的差額。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record flow reference temperature and pressure, comparing compressor inlet and outlet states with electrical power. Cross-check air balance using storage-pressure change rather than treating transient filling as a steady average. Close inlet mass flow against stored-air mass increase and separately identify differences caused by heating and leakage. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以空氣供應與壓縮功編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。記錄流量換算的參考溫壓，對照壓縮機入口出口狀態和電功率；用儲氣壓力變化核對總氣量平衡，避免把瞬時充氣量當長期平均。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for air supply and compression work, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Record flow reference temperature and pressure, comparing compressor inlet and outlet states with electrical power. Cross-check air balance using storage-pressure change rather than treating transient filling as a steady average.","failure":"注意干擾：壓縮熱若未散去，等溫假設會低估功率；漏氣又使供氣量不等於有效排水量。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Incomplete heat rejection makes the isothermal estimate optimistic, and leakage separates supplied air from effective displacement. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b224-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"記錄流量換算的參考溫壓，對照壓縮機入口出口狀態和電功率；用儲氣壓力變化核對總氣量平衡，避免把瞬時充氣量當長期平均。用入口質量流率與儲氣質量增量閉合空氣平衡，另列溫升和漏氣造成的差額。","textEn":"Record flow reference temperature and pressure, comparing compressor inlet and outlet states with electrical power. Cross-check air balance using storage-pressure change rather than treating transient filling as a steady average. Close inlet mass flow against stored-air mass increase and separately identify differences caused by heating and leakage.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b224-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以空氣供應與壓縮功編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。記錄流量換算的參考溫壓，對照壓縮機入口出口狀態和電功率；用儲氣壓力變化核對總氣量平衡，避免把瞬時充氣量當長期平均。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for air supply and compression work, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Record flow reference temperature and pressure, comparing compressor inlet and outlet states with electrical power. Cross-check air balance using storage-pressure change rather than treating transient filling as a steady average.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「空氣供應與壓縮功」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Air supply and compression work\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","備援壓縮機能啟動就保證末端閥件取得足夠供氣。","記錄流量換算的參考溫壓，對照壓縮機入口出口狀態和電功率；用儲氣壓力變化核對總氣量平衡，避免把瞬時充氣量當長期平均。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A starting standby compressor guarantees sufficient air delivery at terminal valves.","Record flow reference temperature and pressure, comparing compressor inlet and outlet states with electrical power."],"answer":2,"explanation":"記錄流量換算的參考溫壓，對照壓縮機入口出口狀態和電功率；用儲氣壓力變化核對總氣量平衡，避免把瞬時充氣量當長期平均。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record flow reference temperature and pressure, comparing compressor inlet and outlet states with electrical power. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b224-v15-12","title":"空氣供應與壓縮功：失效診斷","titleEn":"Air supply and compression work: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b224-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「空氣供應與壓縮功」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Air supply and compression work” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"壓縮熱若未散去，等溫假設會低估功率；漏氣又使供氣量不等於有效排水量。把氣量和門體位移直接一對一換算，會漏掉可壓縮儲能。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Incomplete heat rejection makes the isothermal estimate optimistic, and leakage separates supplied air from effective displacement. Equating air volume directly with gate movement ignores compressible energy stored in the system. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：把氣量和門體位移直接一對一換算，會漏掉可壓縮儲能。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Equating air volume directly with gate movement ignores compressible energy stored in the system.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「供氣量增加一定等比例增加浮門的排水體積。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Increasing supplied air always proportionally increases the gates displaced water volume.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b224-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"壓縮熱若未散去，等溫假設會低估功率；漏氣又使供氣量不等於有效排水量。把氣量和門體位移直接一對一換算，會漏掉可壓縮儲能。","textEn":"Incomplete heat rejection makes the isothermal estimate optimistic, and leakage separates supplied air from effective displacement. Equating air volume directly with gate movement ignores compressible energy stored in the system.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b224-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「空氣供應與壓縮功」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Air supply and compression work\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["壓縮熱若未散去，等溫假設會低估功率；漏氣又使供氣量不等於有效排水量。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","只要有兩座鉸鏈，每座就永遠承受一半荷載。"],"optionsEn":["Incomplete heat rejection makes the isothermal estimate optimistic, and leakage separates supplied air from effective displacement.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","With two hinges each always carries exactly half the applied load."],"answer":0,"explanation":"壓縮熱若未散去，等溫假設會低估功率；漏氣又使供氣量不等於有效排水量。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Incomplete heat rejection makes the isothermal estimate optimistic, and leakage separates supplied air from effective displacement. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b224-v15-13","title":"鉸座荷載分配：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Hinge reaction distribution: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b224-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「鉸座荷載分配」如何影響威尼斯 MOSE 防潮系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Hinge reaction distribution” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Venice MOSE flood barriers”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"多鉸座承受門體合力時，構件剛度與安裝高差控制分配，均分只適用對稱理想情況。局部接觸與變形會讓一個鉸座先承載。 假設兩鉸座間距8 m、合力6 MN偏心1 m，靜力反力R1=3+6/8=3.75 MN、R2=2.25 MN；限剛性門體與平面荷載。 把兩鉸座固定均分會低估偏心側承載，腐蝕或間隙改變又可能造成重新分配。只有總合力監測，無法辨識單個連接件的局部超載。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「鉸座荷載分配」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"When several hinges share a gate resultant, stiffness and installation offsets govern distribution. Equal sharing is an ideal symmetric case; local contact and deformation may load one support first. Assume hinge spacing 8 m and resultant 6 MN offset 1 m. Reactions are R1=3+6/8=3.75 MN and R2=2.25 MN, for a rigid gate under planar loading. Fixed equal sharing underestimates the eccentric side, while corrosion and clearance changes redistribute load. Monitoring total resultant alone cannot identify overload in one individual connection or bearing. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Hinge reaction distribution” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設兩鉸座間距8 m、合力6 MN偏心1 m，靜力反力R1=3+6/8=3.75 MN、R2=2.25 MN；限剛性門體與平面荷載。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume hinge spacing 8 m and resultant 6 MN offset 1 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要有兩座鉸鏈，每座就永遠承受一半荷載。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"With two hinges each always carries exactly half the applied load.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「鉸座荷載分配」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Hinge reaction distribution”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b224-v15-13-k1","title":"鉸座荷載分配","titleEn":"Hinge reaction distribution","text":"多鉸座承受門體合力時，構件剛度與安裝高差控制分配，均分只適用對稱理想情況。局部接觸與變形會讓一個鉸座先承載。","textEn":"When several hinges share a gate resultant, stiffness and installation offsets govern distribution. Equal sharing is an ideal symmetric case; local contact and deformation may load one support first.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b224-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要有兩座鉸鏈，每座就永遠承受一半荷載。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: With two hinges each always carries exactly half the applied load. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「鉸座荷載分配」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Hinge reaction distribution\" is correct?","options":["只要有兩座鉸鏈，每座就永遠承受一半荷載。","多鉸座承受門體合力時，構件剛度與安裝高差控制分配，均分只適用對稱理想情況。","浮門乾態自振週期可以直接當成水中的自振週期。"],"optionsEn":["With two hinges each always carries exactly half the applied load.","When several hinges share a gate resultant, stiffness and installation offsets govern distribution.","A dry gate natural period can directly represent its wet natural period."],"answer":1,"explanation":"多鉸座承受門體合力時，構件剛度與安裝高差控制分配，均分只適用對稱理想情況。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"When several hinges share a gate resultant, stiffness and installation offsets govern distribution. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b224-v15-14","title":"鉸座荷載分配：定量估算","titleEn":"Hinge reaction distribution: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b224-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「鉸座荷載分配」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Hinge reaction distribution” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設兩鉸座間距8 m、合力6 MN偏心1 m，靜力反力R1=3+6/8=3.75 MN、R2=2.25 MN；限剛性門體與平面荷載。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume hinge spacing 8 m and resultant 6 MN offset 1 m. Reactions are R1=3+6/8=3.75 MN and R2=2.25 MN, for a rigid gate under planar loading. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：把鉸座幾何、軸承間隙和應變訊號一起核對，確認反力和等於外載且力矩平衡；不同門角分別作圖，找出接觸改變的轉折。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare hinge geometry, bearing clearance and strain, checking that reactions sum to applied load and balance its moment.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b224-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設兩鉸座間距8 m、合力6 MN偏心1 m，靜力反力R1=3+6/8=3.75 MN、R2=2.25 MN；限剛性門體與平面荷載。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume hinge spacing 8 m and resultant 6 MN offset 1 m. Reactions are R1=3+6/8=3.75 MN and R2=2.25 MN, for a rigid gate under planar loading.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b224-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「鉸座荷載分配」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Hinge reaction distribution\", which statement holds?","options":["海口關閉後，潟湖內水量就必定保持固定。","壓力感測器讀數一致就證明共同取壓管沒有問題。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設兩鉸座間距8 m、合力6 MN偏心1 m，靜力反力R1=3+6/8=3.75 MN、R2=2.25 MN。"],"optionsEn":["Once the inlets close the lagoon water volume must remain constant.","Matching pressure readings prove the shared impulse connection has no defect.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume hinge spacing 8 m and resultant 6 MN offset 1 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設兩鉸座間距8 m、合力6 MN偏心1 m，靜力反力R1=3+6/8=3.75 MN、R2=2.25 MN；限剛性門體與平面荷載。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume hinge spacing 8 m and resultant 6 MN offset 1 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b224-v15-15","title":"鉸座荷載分配：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Hinge reaction distribution: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b224-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「鉸座荷載分配」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Hinge reaction distribution” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"把鉸座幾何、軸承間隙和應變訊號一起核對，確認反力和等於外載且力矩平衡；不同門角分別作圖，找出接觸改變的轉折。將左右反力差與外載偏心量對照，檢查殘差是否跟門角或軸承接觸變化一致。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare hinge geometry, bearing clearance and strain, checking that reactions sum to applied load and balance its moment. Plot separate gate angles to identify changes in contact. Compare reaction difference with load eccentricity and test whether residuals track gate angle or changes in bearing contact. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以鉸座荷載分配編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。把鉸座幾何、軸承間隙和應變訊號一起核對，確認反力和等於外載且力矩平衡；不同門角分別作圖，找出接觸改變的轉折。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for hinge reaction distribution, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Compare hinge geometry, bearing clearance and strain, checking that reactions sum to applied load and balance its moment. Plot separate gate angles to identify changes in contact.","failure":"注意干擾：把兩鉸座固定均分會低估偏心側承載，腐蝕或間隙改變又可能造成重新分配。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Fixed equal sharing underestimates the eccentric side, while corrosion and clearance changes redistribute load. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b224-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"把鉸座幾何、軸承間隙和應變訊號一起核對，確認反力和等於外載且力矩平衡；不同門角分別作圖，找出接觸改變的轉折。將左右反力差與外載偏心量對照，檢查殘差是否跟門角或軸承接觸變化一致。","textEn":"Compare hinge geometry, bearing clearance and strain, checking that reactions sum to applied load and balance its moment. Plot separate gate angles to identify changes in contact. Compare reaction difference with load eccentricity and test whether residuals track gate angle or changes in bearing contact.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b224-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以鉸座荷載分配編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。把鉸座幾何、軸承間隙和應變訊號一起核對，確認反力和等於外載且力矩平衡；不同門角分別作圖，找出接觸改變的轉折。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for hinge reaction distribution, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Compare hinge geometry, bearing clearance and strain, checking that reactions sum to applied load and balance its moment. Plot separate gate angles to identify changes in contact.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「鉸座荷載分配」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Hinge reaction distribution\"?","options":["把鉸座幾何、軸承間隙和應變訊號一起核對，確認反力和等於外載且力矩平衡；不同門角分別作圖，找出接觸改變的轉折。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","總浮力大於自重就能直接決定翻板的唯一平衡角。"],"optionsEn":["Compare hinge geometry, bearing clearance and strain, checking that reactions sum to applied load and balance its moment.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Buoyancy exceeding weight directly determines the unique flap equilibrium angle."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把鉸座幾何、軸承間隙和應變訊號一起核對，確認反力和等於外載且力矩平衡；不同門角分別作圖，找出接觸改變的轉折。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare hinge geometry, bearing clearance and strain, checking that reactions sum to applied load and balance its moment. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b224-v15-16","title":"鉸座荷載分配：失效診斷","titleEn":"Hinge reaction distribution: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b224-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「鉸座荷載分配」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Hinge reaction distribution” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把兩鉸座固定均分會低估偏心側承載，腐蝕或間隙改變又可能造成重新分配。只有總合力監測，無法辨識單個連接件的局部超載。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Fixed equal sharing underestimates the eccentric side, while corrosion and clearance changes redistribute load. Monitoring total resultant alone cannot identify overload in one individual connection or bearing. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：只有總合力監測，無法辨識單個連接件的局部超載。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Monitoring total resultant alone cannot identify overload in one individual connection or bearing.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要有兩座鉸鏈，每座就永遠承受一半荷載。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"With two hinges each always carries exactly half the applied load.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b224-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把兩鉸座固定均分會低估偏心側承載，腐蝕或間隙改變又可能造成重新分配。只有總合力監測，無法辨識單個連接件的局部超載。","textEn":"Fixed equal sharing underestimates the eccentric side, while corrosion and clearance changes redistribute load. Monitoring total resultant alone cannot identify overload in one individual connection or bearing.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b224-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「鉸座荷載分配」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Hinge reaction distribution\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","把兩鉸座固定均分會低估偏心側承載，腐蝕或間隙改變又可能造成重新分配。","浮門乾態自振週期可以直接當成水中的自振週期。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Fixed equal sharing underestimates the eccentric side, while corrosion and clearance changes redistribute load.","A dry gate natural period can directly represent its wet natural period."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把兩鉸座固定均分會低估偏心側承載，腐蝕或間隙改變又可能造成重新分配。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Fixed equal sharing underestimates the eccentric side, while corrosion and clearance changes redistribute load. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b224-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「波浪激振與自振」與「相鄰門片相對位移」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Wave excitation and natural period\" and \"Relative motion between gates\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b224-v15-17","title":"波浪激振與自振：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Wave excitation and natural period: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b224-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「波浪激振與自振」如何影響威尼斯 MOSE 防潮系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Wave excitation and natural period” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Venice MOSE flood barriers”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"浮動門體具有轉動慣性、復原剛度與水體附加慣性，波浪頻率接近自振時可能放大運動。乾態模態不能直接替代濕態動力特性。 假設含附加水慣性的I=8×10⁸ kg·m²、線性轉動剛度K=2×10⁸ N·m/rad，T=2π√(I/K)=12.566 s；限小擾動。 大角度運動會改變浮力剛度，破壞線性週期假設；相鄰門片的流體耦合也會產生集體模態。以單片門的小振幅結果代表整列，可能漏掉相對運動。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「波浪激振與自振」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A buoyant gate has rotational inertia, restoring stiffness and added hydrodynamic inertia. Excitation near its natural frequency can amplify motion, so dry structural modes cannot replace wet dynamic properties. Assume inertia including added water I=8×10⁸ kg·m² and linear rotational stiffness K=2×10⁸ N·m/rad. T=2π√(I/K)=12.566 s, for small disturbances. Large angles alter restoring stiffness and invalidate a linear period. Hydrodynamic coupling produces collective modes, so a single-gate small-motion result can miss relative movement across the full barrier. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Wave excitation and natural period” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設含附加水慣性的I=8×10⁸ kg·m²、線性轉動剛度K=2×10⁸ N·m/rad，T=2π√(I/K)=12.566 s；限小擾動。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume inertia including added water I=8×10⁸ kg·m² and linear rotational stiffness K=2×10⁸ N·m/rad.","failure":"常見誤解：「浮門乾態自振週期可以直接當成水中的自振週期。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A dry gate natural period can directly represent its wet natural period.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「波浪激振與自振」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Wave excitation and natural period”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b224-v15-17-k1","title":"波浪激振與自振","titleEn":"Wave excitation and natural period","text":"浮動門體具有轉動慣性、復原剛度與水體附加慣性，波浪頻率接近自振時可能放大運動。乾態模態不能直接替代濕態動力特性。","textEn":"A buoyant gate has rotational inertia, restoring stiffness and added hydrodynamic inertia. Excitation near its natural frequency can amplify motion, so dry structural modes cannot replace wet dynamic properties.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b224-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：浮門乾態自振週期可以直接當成水中的自振週期。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A dry gate natural period can directly represent its wet natural period. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「波浪激振與自振」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Wave excitation and natural period\" is correct?","options":["浮門乾態自振週期可以直接當成水中的自振週期。","兩片門振幅相同就表示它們沒有相對運動。","浮動門體具有轉動慣性、復原剛度與水體附加慣性，波浪頻率接近自振時可能放大運動。"],"optionsEn":["A dry gate natural period can directly represent its wet natural period.","Two gates with equal amplitudes have no relative motion between them.","A buoyant gate has rotational inertia, restoring stiffness and added hydrodynamic inertia."],"answer":2,"explanation":"浮動門體具有轉動慣性、復原剛度與水體附加慣性，波浪頻率接近自振時可能放大運動。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A buoyant gate has rotational inertia, restoring stiffness and added hydrodynamic inertia. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b224-v15-18","title":"波浪激振與自振：定量估算","titleEn":"Wave excitation and natural period: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b224-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「波浪激振與自振」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Wave excitation and natural period” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設含附加水慣性的I=8×10⁸ kg·m²、線性轉動剛度K=2×10⁸ N·m/rad，T=2π√(I/K)=12.566 s；限小擾動。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume inertia including added water I=8×10⁸ kg·m² and linear rotational stiffness K=2×10⁸ N·m/rad. T=2π√(I/K)=12.566 s, for small disturbances. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較門角和波面頻譜，辨認相位及阻尼而非只找相同頻率；在不同水深重估附加慣性，確認觀測峰值不是感測器安裝共振。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare angle and wave spectra, examining phase and damping rather than frequency coincidence alone.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b224-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設含附加水慣性的I=8×10⁸ kg·m²、線性轉動剛度K=2×10⁸ N·m/rad，T=2π√(I/K)=12.566 s；限小擾動。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume inertia including added water I=8×10⁸ kg·m² and linear rotational stiffness K=2×10⁸ N·m/rad. T=2π√(I/K)=12.566 s, for small disturbances.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b224-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「波浪激振與自振」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Wave excitation and natural period\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設含附加水慣性的I=8×10⁸ kg·m²、線性轉動剛度K=2×10⁸ N·m/rad，T=2π√(I/K)=12.566 s。","平均鹽度降低就證明底層高鹽水已完全排出。","備援壓縮機能啟動就保證末端閥件取得足夠供氣。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume inertia including added water I=8×10⁸ kg·m² and linear rotational stiffness K=2×10⁸ N·m/rad.","Lower mean salinity proves that all saline bottom water has been removed.","A starting standby compressor guarantees sufficient air delivery at terminal valves."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設含附加水慣性的I=8×10⁸ kg·m²、線性轉動剛度K=2×10⁸ N·m/rad，T=2π√(I/K)=12.566 s；限小擾動。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume inertia including added water I=8×10⁸ kg·m² and linear rotational stiffness K=2×10⁸ N·m/rad. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b224-v15-19","title":"波浪激振與自振：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Wave excitation and natural period: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b224-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「波浪激振與自振」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Wave excitation and natural period” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較門角和波面頻譜，辨認相位及阻尼而非只找相同頻率；在不同水深重估附加慣性，確認觀測峰值不是感測器安裝共振。以相位跨越與衰減包絡交叉確認共振，而非只用頻譜上單一尖峰作判定。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare angle and wave spectra, examining phase and damping rather than frequency coincidence alone. Reassess added inertia at different depths and rule out resonance of sensor mountings. Confirm resonance through phase transition and decay envelopes rather than relying on one isolated spectral peak. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以波浪激振與自振編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。比較門角和波面頻譜，辨認相位及阻尼而非只找相同頻率；在不同水深重估附加慣性，確認觀測峰值不是感測器安裝共振。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for wave excitation and natural period, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Compare angle and wave spectra, examining phase and damping rather than frequency coincidence alone. Reassess added inertia at different depths and rule out resonance of sensor mountings.","failure":"注意干擾：大角度運動會改變浮力剛度，破壞線性週期假設；相鄰門片的流體耦合也會產生集體模態。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Large angles alter restoring stiffness and invalidate a linear period. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b224-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較門角和波面頻譜，辨認相位及阻尼而非只找相同頻率；在不同水深重估附加慣性，確認觀測峰值不是感測器安裝共振。以相位跨越與衰減包絡交叉確認共振，而非只用頻譜上單一尖峰作判定。","textEn":"Compare angle and wave spectra, examining phase and damping rather than frequency coincidence alone. Reassess added inertia at different depths and rule out resonance of sensor mountings. Confirm resonance through phase transition and decay envelopes rather than relying on one isolated spectral peak.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b224-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以波浪激振與自振編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。比較門角和波面頻譜，辨認相位及阻尼而非只找相同頻率；在不同水深重估附加慣性，確認觀測峰值不是感測器安裝共振。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for wave excitation and natural period, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Compare angle and wave spectra, examining phase and damping rather than frequency coincidence alone. Reassess added inertia at different depths and rule out resonance of sensor mountings.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「波浪激振與自振」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Wave excitation and natural period\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","比較門角和波面頻譜，辨認相位及阻尼而非只找相同頻率；在不同水深重估附加慣性，確認觀測峰值不是感測器安裝共振。","氣體狀態換算可以直接用表壓取代絕對壓力。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Compare angle and wave spectra, examining phase and damping rather than frequency coincidence alone.","Gas-state calculations can directly substitute gauge pressure for absolute pressure."],"answer":1,"explanation":"比較門角和波面頻譜，辨認相位及阻尼而非只找相同頻率；在不同水深重估附加慣性，確認觀測峰值不是感測器安裝共振。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare angle and wave spectra, examining phase and damping rather than frequency coincidence alone. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b224-v15-20","title":"波浪激振與自振：失效診斷","titleEn":"Wave excitation and natural period: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b224-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「波浪激振與自振」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Wave excitation and natural period” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"大角度運動會改變浮力剛度，破壞線性週期假設；相鄰門片的流體耦合也會產生集體模態。以單片門的小振幅結果代表整列，可能漏掉相對運動。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Large angles alter restoring stiffness and invalidate a linear period. Hydrodynamic coupling produces collective modes, so a single-gate small-motion result can miss relative movement across the full barrier. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：以單片門的小振幅結果代表整列，可能漏掉相對運動。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Hydrodynamic coupling produces collective modes, so a single-gate small-motion result can miss relative movement across the full barrier.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「浮門乾態自振週期可以直接當成水中的自振週期。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A dry gate natural period can directly represent its wet natural period.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b224-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"大角度運動會改變浮力剛度，破壞線性週期假設；相鄰門片的流體耦合也會產生集體模態。以單片門的小振幅結果代表整列，可能漏掉相對運動。","textEn":"Large angles alter restoring stiffness and invalidate a linear period. Hydrodynamic coupling produces collective modes, so a single-gate small-motion result can miss relative movement across the full barrier.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b224-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「波浪激振與自振」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Wave excitation and natural period\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","兩片門振幅相同就表示它們沒有相對運動。","大角度運動會改變浮力剛度，破壞線性週期假設；相鄰門片的流體耦合也會產生集體模態。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Two gates with equal amplitudes have no relative motion between them.","Large angles alter restoring stiffness and invalidate a linear period."],"answer":2,"explanation":"大角度運動會改變浮力剛度，破壞線性週期假設；相鄰門片的流體耦合也會產生集體模態。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Large angles alter restoring stiffness and invalidate a linear period. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b224-v15-21","title":"相鄰門片相對位移：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Relative motion between gates: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b224-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「相鄰門片相對位移」如何影響威尼斯 MOSE 防潮系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Relative motion between gates” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Venice MOSE flood barriers”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"兩片門同方向移動時，相對間隙可能很小；反相時則可能最大。接觸風險取決於相對運動與公差，不能只看每片門的最大位移。 假設兩門邊緣振幅各0.04 m、相位差120°，相對振幅√(A1²+A2²−2A1A2cosφ)=0.06928 m；同頻正弦近似。 兩套感測器若時鐘不一致，可能製造假的反相訊號。反之只存最大振幅會丟失相位，無法判定是否同時接近，造成不必要或不足的碰撞評估。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「相鄰門片相對位移」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Two gates moving together can have small relative displacement, while opposing phases can maximize it. Contact risk depends on relative motion and tolerances, not each gate maximum independently. Assume edge amplitudes 0.04 m each and phase difference 120°. Relative amplitude √(A1²+A2²−2A1A2cosφ)=0.06928 m, for equal-frequency sinusoidal motion. Unsynchronized clocks can create a false out-of-phase response. Saving only maximum amplitudes loses phase, preventing determination of simultaneous approach and producing either excessive or insufficient collision assessment. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Relative motion between gates” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設兩門邊緣振幅各0.04 m、相位差120°，相對振幅√(A1²+A2²−2A1A2cosφ)=0.06928 m；同頻正弦近似。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume edge amplitudes 0.04 m each and phase difference 120°.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩片門振幅相同就表示它們沒有相對運動。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Two gates with equal amplitudes have no relative motion between them.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「相鄰門片相對位移」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Relative motion between gates”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b224-v15-21-k1","title":"相鄰門片相對位移","titleEn":"Relative motion between gates","text":"兩片門同方向移動時，相對間隙可能很小；反相時則可能最大。接觸風險取決於相對運動與公差，不能只看每片門的最大位移。","textEn":"Two gates moving together can have small relative displacement, while opposing phases can maximize it. Contact risk depends on relative motion and tolerances, not each gate maximum independently.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b224-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩片門振幅相同就表示它們沒有相對運動。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Two gates with equal amplitudes have no relative motion between them. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「相鄰門片相對位移」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Relative motion between gates\" is correct?","options":["兩片門同方向移動時，相對間隙可能很小；反相時則可能最大。","兩片門振幅相同就表示它們沒有相對運動。","海口關閉後，潟湖內水量就必定保持固定。"],"optionsEn":["Two gates moving together can have small relative displacement, while opposing phases can maximize it.","Two gates with equal amplitudes have no relative motion between them.","Once the inlets close the lagoon water volume must remain constant."],"answer":0,"explanation":"兩片門同方向移動時，相對間隙可能很小；反相時則可能最大。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Two gates moving together can have small relative displacement, while opposing phases can maximize it. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b224-v15-22","title":"相鄰門片相對位移：定量估算","titleEn":"Relative motion between gates: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b224-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「相鄰門片相對位移」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Relative motion between gates” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設兩門邊緣振幅各0.04 m、相位差120°，相對振幅√(A1²+A2²−2A1A2cosφ)=0.06928 m；同頻正弦近似。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume edge amplitudes 0.04 m each and phase difference 120°. Relative amplitude √(A1²+A2²−2A1A2cosφ)=0.06928 m, for equal-frequency sinusoidal motion. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步量測相鄰門角並換算同一高度的邊緣位移，保留相位資訊；把靜態公差、熱變形與動態間隙分列，檢查時間同步誤差。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Synchronize adjacent gate angles and convert them to edge displacement at one elevation.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b224-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設兩門邊緣振幅各0.04 m、相位差120°，相對振幅√(A1²+A2²−2A1A2cosφ)=0.06928 m；同頻正弦近似。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume edge amplitudes 0.04 m each and phase difference 120°. Relative amplitude √(A1²+A2²−2A1A2cosφ)=0.06928 m, for equal-frequency sinusoidal motion.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b224-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「相鄰門片相對位移」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Relative motion between gates\", which statement holds?","options":["壓力感測器讀數一致就證明共同取壓管沒有問題。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設兩門邊緣振幅各0.04 m、相位差120°，相對振幅√(A1²+A2²−2A1A2cosφ)=0.06928 m。","總浮力大於自重就能直接決定翻板的唯一平衡角。"],"optionsEn":["Matching pressure readings prove the shared impulse connection has no defect.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume edge amplitudes 0.04 m each and phase difference 120°.","Buoyancy exceeding weight directly determines the unique flap equilibrium angle."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設兩門邊緣振幅各0.04 m、相位差120°，相對振幅√(A1²+A2²−2A1A2cosφ)=0.06928 m；同頻正弦近似。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume edge amplitudes 0.04 m each and phase difference 120°. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b224-v15-23","title":"相鄰門片相對位移：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Relative motion between gates: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b224-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「相鄰門片相對位移」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Relative motion between gates” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步量測相鄰門角並換算同一高度的邊緣位移，保留相位資訊；把靜態公差、熱變形與動態間隙分列，檢查時間同步誤差。把兩邊位移原始時序直接相減，對照相位公式並量化時間戳誤差對結果的影響。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Synchronize adjacent gate angles and convert them to edge displacement at one elevation. Retain phase and separate static tolerance, thermal distortion and dynamic clearance, checking synchronization error. Subtract raw edge-displacement histories directly, compare with the phase formula and quantify sensitivity to timestamp error. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以相鄰門片相對位移編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。同步量測相鄰門角並換算同一高度的邊緣位移，保留相位資訊；把靜態公差、熱變形與動態間隙分列，檢查時間同步誤差。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for relative motion between gates, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Synchronize adjacent gate angles and convert them to edge displacement at one elevation. Retain phase and separate static tolerance, thermal distortion and dynamic clearance, checking synchronization error.","failure":"注意干擾：兩套感測器若時鐘不一致，可能製造假的反相訊號。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Unsynchronized clocks can create a false out-of-phase response. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b224-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步量測相鄰門角並換算同一高度的邊緣位移，保留相位資訊；把靜態公差、熱變形與動態間隙分列，檢查時間同步誤差。把兩邊位移原始時序直接相減，對照相位公式並量化時間戳誤差對結果的影響。","textEn":"Synchronize adjacent gate angles and convert them to edge displacement at one elevation. Retain phase and separate static tolerance, thermal distortion and dynamic clearance, checking synchronization error. Subtract raw edge-displacement histories directly, compare with the phase formula and quantify sensitivity to timestamp error.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b224-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以相鄰門片相對位移編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。同步量測相鄰門角並換算同一高度的邊緣位移，保留相位資訊；把靜態公差、熱變形與動態間隙分列，檢查時間同步誤差。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for relative motion between gates, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Synchronize adjacent gate angles and convert them to edge displacement at one elevation. Retain phase and separate static tolerance, thermal distortion and dynamic clearance, checking synchronization error.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「相鄰門片相對位移」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Relative motion between gates\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","供氣量增加一定等比例增加浮門的排水體積。","同步量測相鄰門角並換算同一高度的邊緣位移，保留相位資訊；把靜態公差、熱變形與動態間隙分列，檢查時間同步誤差。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Increasing supplied air always proportionally increases the gates displaced water volume.","Synchronize adjacent gate angles and convert them to edge displacement at one elevation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"同步量測相鄰門角並換算同一高度的邊緣位移，保留相位資訊；把靜態公差、熱變形與動態間隙分列，檢查時間同步誤差。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Synchronize adjacent gate angles and convert them to edge displacement at one elevation. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b224-v15-24","title":"相鄰門片相對位移：失效診斷","titleEn":"Relative motion between gates: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b224-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「相鄰門片相對位移」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Relative motion between gates” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"兩套感測器若時鐘不一致，可能製造假的反相訊號。反之只存最大振幅會丟失相位，無法判定是否同時接近，造成不必要或不足的碰撞評估。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Unsynchronized clocks can create a false out-of-phase response. Saving only maximum amplitudes loses phase, preventing determination of simultaneous approach and producing either excessive or insufficient collision assessment. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：反之只存最大振幅會丟失相位，無法判定是否同時接近，造成不必要或不足的碰撞評估。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Saving only maximum amplitudes loses phase, preventing determination of simultaneous approach and producing either excessive or insufficient collision assessment.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩片門振幅相同就表示它們沒有相對運動。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Two gates with equal amplitudes have no relative motion between them.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b224-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"兩套感測器若時鐘不一致，可能製造假的反相訊號。反之只存最大振幅會丟失相位，無法判定是否同時接近，造成不必要或不足的碰撞評估。","textEn":"Unsynchronized clocks can create a false out-of-phase response. Saving only maximum amplitudes loses phase, preventing determination of simultaneous approach and producing either excessive or insufficient collision assessment.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b224-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「相鄰門片相對位移」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Relative motion between gates\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["兩套感測器若時鐘不一致，可能製造假的反相訊號。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","海口關閉後，潟湖內水量就必定保持固定。"],"optionsEn":["Unsynchronized clocks can create a false out-of-phase response.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Once the inlets close the lagoon water volume must remain constant."],"answer":0,"explanation":"兩套感測器若時鐘不一致，可能製造假的反相訊號。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Unsynchronized clocks can create a false out-of-phase response. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b224-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「關閉潟湖降雨收支」與「鹽分混合與交換」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Rainfall balance in an isolated lagoon\" and \"Salinity mixing and exchange\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b224-v15-25","title":"關閉潟湖降雨收支：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Rainfall balance in an isolated lagoon: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b224-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「關閉潟湖降雨收支」如何影響威尼斯 MOSE 防潮系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Rainfall balance in an isolated lagoon” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Venice MOSE flood barriers”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"防潮時海口交換減少，但潟湖降雨和陸域排水仍在加入水量。水面面積使水位對體積敏感度不同，內部風致增水又會打破均勻水位假設。 假設封閉水面100 km²、降雨20 mm且全部直接入水，增量2 million m³、水位上升0.02 m；未含陸域逕流、蒸發或漏流。 將整個流域雨量直接乘潟湖面積會混淆陸地與水面貢獻，地下水和支流也有延遲。只看封閉後平均水位，可能漏掉城市沿岸的局部高水位。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「關閉潟湖降雨收支」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Reducing inlet exchange does not stop rainfall or land drainage into the lagoon. Surface area controls stage sensitivity to volume, while wind setup can invalidate a uniform water level assumption. Assume isolated surface area 100 km² and direct rainfall 20 mm. Added volume is 2 million m³ and mean rise 0.02 m, excluding land runoff, evaporation and leakage. Multiplying catchment rain by lagoon area confuses land and open-water contributions, while groundwater and tributaries are delayed. Mean lagoon level can miss locally higher levels along urban shores. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Rainfall balance in an isolated lagoon” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設封閉水面100 km²、降雨20 mm且全部直接入水，增量2 million m³、水位上升0.02 m；未含陸域逕流、蒸發或漏流。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume isolated surface area 100 km² and direct rainfall 20 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「海口關閉後，潟湖內水量就必定保持固定。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Once the inlets close the lagoon water volume must remain constant.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「關閉潟湖降雨收支」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Rainfall balance in an isolated lagoon”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b224-v15-25-k1","title":"關閉潟湖降雨收支","titleEn":"Rainfall balance in an isolated lagoon","text":"防潮時海口交換減少，但潟湖降雨和陸域排水仍在加入水量。水面面積使水位對體積敏感度不同，內部風致增水又會打破均勻水位假設。","textEn":"Reducing inlet exchange does not stop rainfall or land drainage into the lagoon. Surface area controls stage sensitivity to volume, while wind setup can invalidate a uniform water level assumption.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b224-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：海口關閉後，潟湖內水量就必定保持固定。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Once the inlets close the lagoon water volume must remain constant. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「關閉潟湖降雨收支」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Rainfall balance in an isolated lagoon\" is correct?","options":["海口關閉後，潟湖內水量就必定保持固定。","防潮時海口交換減少，但潟湖降雨和陸域排水仍在加入水量。","平均鹽度降低就證明底層高鹽水已完全排出。"],"optionsEn":["Once the inlets close the lagoon water volume must remain constant.","Reducing inlet exchange does not stop rainfall or land drainage into the lagoon.","Lower mean salinity proves that all saline bottom water has been removed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"防潮時海口交換減少，但潟湖降雨和陸域排水仍在加入水量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Reducing inlet exchange does not stop rainfall or land drainage into the lagoon. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b224-v15-26","title":"關閉潟湖降雨收支：定量估算","titleEn":"Rainfall balance in an isolated lagoon: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b224-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「關閉潟湖降雨收支」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Rainfall balance in an isolated lagoon” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設封閉水面100 km²、降雨20 mm且全部直接入水，增量2 million m³、水位上升0.02 m；未含陸域逕流、蒸發或漏流。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume isolated surface area 100 km² and direct rainfall 20 mm. Added volume is 2 million m³ and mean rise 0.02 m, excluding land runoff, evaporation and leakage. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：對照雨量雷達、雨量站和內外潮位，建立分時水量平衡；用不同方位水位站辨識風致傾斜，避免把單站升高全歸因於降雨。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare radar, rain gauges and internal and external levels in a time-resolved balance.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b224-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設封閉水面100 km²、降雨20 mm且全部直接入水，增量2 million m³、水位上升0.02 m；未含陸域逕流、蒸發或漏流。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume isolated surface area 100 km² and direct rainfall 20 mm. Added volume is 2 million m³ and mean rise 0.02 m, excluding land runoff, evaporation and leakage.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b224-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「關閉潟湖降雨收支」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Rainfall balance in an isolated lagoon\", which statement holds?","options":["備援壓縮機能啟動就保證末端閥件取得足夠供氣。","氣體狀態換算可以直接用表壓取代絕對壓力。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設封閉水面100 km²、降雨20 mm且全部直接入水，增量2 million m³、水位上升0.02 m。"],"optionsEn":["A starting standby compressor guarantees sufficient air delivery at terminal valves.","Gas-state calculations can directly substitute gauge pressure for absolute pressure.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume isolated surface area 100 km² and direct rainfall 20 mm."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設封閉水面100 km²、降雨20 mm且全部直接入水，增量2 million m³、水位上升0.02 m；未含陸域逕流、蒸發或漏流。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume isolated surface area 100 km² and direct rainfall 20 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b224-v15-27","title":"關閉潟湖降雨收支：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Rainfall balance in an isolated lagoon: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b224-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「關閉潟湖降雨收支」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Rainfall balance in an isolated lagoon” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"對照雨量雷達、雨量站和內外潮位，建立分時水量平衡；用不同方位水位站辨識風致傾斜，避免把單站升高全歸因於降雨。將潟湖不同岸邊水位相減辨識風致坡度，再以全域平均驗算降雨增加的總庫容。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare radar, rain gauges and internal and external levels in a time-resolved balance. Use stations on different shores to identify wind setup instead of attributing all local rise to rainfall. Difference shoreline levels to identify wind setup, then use the domain average to check rainfall-related storage increase. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以關閉潟湖降雨收支編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。對照雨量雷達、雨量站和內外潮位，建立分時水量平衡；用不同方位水位站辨識風致傾斜，避免把單站升高全歸因於降雨。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for rainfall balance in an isolated lagoon, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Compare radar, rain gauges and internal and external levels in a time-resolved balance. Use stations on different shores to identify wind setup instead of attributing all local rise to rainfall.","failure":"注意干擾：將整個流域雨量直接乘潟湖面積會混淆陸地與水面貢獻，地下水和支流也有延遲。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Multiplying catchment rain by lagoon area confuses land and open-water contributions, while groundwater and tributaries are delayed. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b224-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"對照雨量雷達、雨量站和內外潮位，建立分時水量平衡；用不同方位水位站辨識風致傾斜，避免把單站升高全歸因於降雨。將潟湖不同岸邊水位相減辨識風致坡度，再以全域平均驗算降雨增加的總庫容。","textEn":"Compare radar, rain gauges and internal and external levels in a time-resolved balance. Use stations on different shores to identify wind setup instead of attributing all local rise to rainfall. Difference shoreline levels to identify wind setup, then use the domain average to check rainfall-related storage increase.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b224-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以關閉潟湖降雨收支編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。對照雨量雷達、雨量站和內外潮位，建立分時水量平衡；用不同方位水位站辨識風致傾斜，避免把單站升高全歸因於降雨。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for rainfall balance in an isolated lagoon, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Compare radar, rain gauges and internal and external levels in a time-resolved balance. Use stations on different shores to identify wind setup instead of attributing all local rise to rainfall.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「關閉潟湖降雨收支」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Rainfall balance in an isolated lagoon\"?","options":["對照雨量雷達、雨量站和內外潮位，建立分時水量平衡；用不同方位水位站辨識風致傾斜，避免把單站升高全歸因於降雨。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","只要有兩座鉸鏈，每座就永遠承受一半荷載。"],"optionsEn":["Compare radar, rain gauges and internal and external levels in a time-resolved balance.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","With two hinges each always carries exactly half the applied load."],"answer":0,"explanation":"對照雨量雷達、雨量站和內外潮位，建立分時水量平衡；用不同方位水位站辨識風致傾斜，避免把單站升高全歸因於降雨。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare radar, rain gauges and internal and external levels in a time-resolved balance. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b224-v15-28","title":"關閉潟湖降雨收支：失效診斷","titleEn":"Rainfall balance in an isolated lagoon: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b224-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「關閉潟湖降雨收支」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Rainfall balance in an isolated lagoon” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"將整個流域雨量直接乘潟湖面積會混淆陸地與水面貢獻，地下水和支流也有延遲。只看封閉後平均水位，可能漏掉城市沿岸的局部高水位。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Multiplying catchment rain by lagoon area confuses land and open-water contributions, while groundwater and tributaries are delayed. Mean lagoon level can miss locally higher levels along urban shores. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：只看封閉後平均水位，可能漏掉城市沿岸的局部高水位。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Mean lagoon level can miss locally higher levels along urban shores.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「海口關閉後，潟湖內水量就必定保持固定。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Once the inlets close the lagoon water volume must remain constant.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b224-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"將整個流域雨量直接乘潟湖面積會混淆陸地與水面貢獻，地下水和支流也有延遲。只看封閉後平均水位，可能漏掉城市沿岸的局部高水位。","textEn":"Multiplying catchment rain by lagoon area confuses land and open-water contributions, while groundwater and tributaries are delayed. Mean lagoon level can miss locally higher levels along urban shores.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b224-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「關閉潟湖降雨收支」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Rainfall balance in an isolated lagoon\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","將整個流域雨量直接乘潟湖面積會混淆陸地與水面貢獻，地下水和支流也有延遲。","平均鹽度降低就證明底層高鹽水已完全排出。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Multiplying catchment rain by lagoon area confuses land and open-water contributions, while groundwater and tributaries are delayed.","Lower mean salinity proves that all saline bottom water has been removed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"將整個流域雨量直接乘潟湖面積會混淆陸地與水面貢獻，地下水和支流也有延遲。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Multiplying catchment rain by lagoon area confuses land and open-water contributions, while groundwater and tributaries are delayed. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b224-v15-29","title":"鹽分混合與交換：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Salinity mixing and exchange: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b224-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「鹽分混合與交換」如何影響威尼斯 MOSE 防潮系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Salinity mixing and exchange” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Venice MOSE flood barriers”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"鹽分守恆可追蹤海水與淡水比例，但潟湖並非瞬間完全混合。底層密度流和局部滯水會讓平均鹽度掩蓋生態差異。 假設初始100 million m³水體鹽度30 g/kg，加入5 million m³淡水，同密度完全混合；新鹽度30×100/105=28.571 g/kg，無蒸發。 底層高鹽水可在表面變淡時仍滯留，造成密度分層並限制氧氣交換。把所有鹽度變化都歸因於門片動作，會漏掉河流、風和蒸發影響。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「鹽分混合與交換」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Salt conservation tracks seawater and freshwater fractions, but a lagoon does not mix instantly. Bottom density currents and stagnant regions allow a mean salinity to conceal ecological variation. Assume 100 million m³ at 30 g/kg plus 5 million m³ freshwater, equal densities and complete mixing. New salinity is 30×100/105=28.571 g/kg, without evaporation. Saline bottom water can remain after surface freshening, maintaining stratification and limiting oxygen exchange. Attributing every salinity change to gate movement overlooks river, wind and evaporation effects. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Salinity mixing and exchange” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設初始100 million m³水體鹽度30 g/kg，加入5 million m³淡水，同密度完全混合；新鹽度30×100/105=28.571 g/kg，無蒸發。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume 100 million m³ at 30 g/kg plus 5 million m³ freshwater, equal densities and complete mixing.","failure":"常見誤解：「平均鹽度降低就證明底層高鹽水已完全排出。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Lower mean salinity proves that all saline bottom water has been removed.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「鹽分混合與交換」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Salinity mixing and exchange”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b224-v15-29-k1","title":"鹽分混合與交換","titleEn":"Salinity mixing and exchange","text":"鹽分守恆可追蹤海水與淡水比例，但潟湖並非瞬間完全混合。底層密度流和局部滯水會讓平均鹽度掩蓋生態差異。","textEn":"Salt conservation tracks seawater and freshwater fractions, but a lagoon does not mix instantly. Bottom density currents and stagnant regions allow a mean salinity to conceal ecological variation.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b224-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：平均鹽度降低就證明底層高鹽水已完全排出。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Lower mean salinity proves that all saline bottom water has been removed. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「鹽分混合與交換」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Salinity mixing and exchange\" is correct?","options":["平均鹽度降低就證明底層高鹽水已完全排出。","壓力感測器讀數一致就證明共同取壓管沒有問題。","鹽分守恆可追蹤海水與淡水比例，但潟湖並非瞬間完全混合。"],"optionsEn":["Lower mean salinity proves that all saline bottom water has been removed.","Matching pressure readings prove the shared impulse connection has no defect.","Salt conservation tracks seawater and freshwater fractions, but a lagoon does not mix instantly."],"answer":2,"explanation":"鹽分守恆可追蹤海水與淡水比例，但潟湖並非瞬間完全混合。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Salt conservation tracks seawater and freshwater fractions, but a lagoon does not mix instantly. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b224-v15-30","title":"鹽分混合與交換：定量估算","titleEn":"Salinity mixing and exchange: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b224-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「鹽分混合與交換」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Salinity mixing and exchange” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設初始100 million m³水體鹽度30 g/kg，加入5 million m³淡水，同密度完全混合；新鹽度30×100/105=28.571 g/kg，無蒸發。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume 100 million m³ at 30 g/kg plus 5 million m³ freshwater, equal densities and complete mixing. New salinity is 30×100/105=28.571 g/kg, without evaporation. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：採集表中底層鹽溫剖面，核對混合前後水量與導電度校正；對照潮相與支流入流，判斷單一平均值是否足以描述鹽分分布。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Sample surface, middle and bottom salinity-temperature profiles and verify volume balance and conductivity calibration.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b224-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設初始100 million m³水體鹽度30 g/kg，加入5 million m³淡水，同密度完全混合；新鹽度30×100/105=28.571 g/kg，無蒸發。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume 100 million m³ at 30 g/kg plus 5 million m³ freshwater, equal densities and complete mixing. New salinity is 30×100/105=28.571 g/kg, without evaporation.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b224-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「鹽分混合與交換」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Salinity mixing and exchange\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設初始100 million m³水體鹽度30 g/kg，加入5 million m³淡水，同密度完全混合。","總浮力大於自重就能直接決定翻板的唯一平衡角。","供氣量增加一定等比例增加浮門的排水體積。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume 100 million m³ at 30 g/kg plus 5 million m³ freshwater, equal densities and complete mixing.","Buoyancy exceeding weight directly determines the unique flap equilibrium angle.","Increasing supplied air always proportionally increases the gates displaced water volume."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設初始100 million m³水體鹽度30 g/kg，加入5 million m³淡水，同密度完全混合；新鹽度30×100/105=28.571 g/kg，無蒸發。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume 100 million m³ at 30 g/kg plus 5 million m³ freshwater, equal densities and complete mixing. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b224-v15-31","title":"鹽分混合與交換：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Salinity mixing and exchange: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b224-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「鹽分混合與交換」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Salinity mixing and exchange” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"採集表中底層鹽溫剖面，核對混合前後水量與導電度校正；對照潮相與支流入流，判斷單一平均值是否足以描述鹽分分布。以各層水量加權鹽度重建總鹽質量，檢查表面淡化是否只是分層而非整體排鹽。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Sample surface, middle and bottom salinity-temperature profiles and verify volume balance and conductivity calibration. Compare tides and tributary inputs to test whether one average adequately describes the distribution. Reconstruct total salt from layer-volume-weighted salinity and check whether surface freshening reflects stratification rather than salt removal. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以鹽分混合與交換編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。採集表中底層鹽溫剖面，核對混合前後水量與導電度校正；對照潮相與支流入流，判斷單一平均值是否足以描述鹽分分布。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for salinity mixing and exchange, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Sample surface, middle and bottom salinity-temperature profiles and verify volume balance and conductivity calibration. Compare tides and tributary inputs to test whether one average adequately describes the distribution.","failure":"注意干擾：底層高鹽水可在表面變淡時仍滯留，造成密度分層並限制氧氣交換。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Saline bottom water can remain after surface freshening, maintaining stratification and limiting oxygen exchange. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b224-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"採集表中底層鹽溫剖面，核對混合前後水量與導電度校正；對照潮相與支流入流，判斷單一平均值是否足以描述鹽分分布。以各層水量加權鹽度重建總鹽質量，檢查表面淡化是否只是分層而非整體排鹽。","textEn":"Sample surface, middle and bottom salinity-temperature profiles and verify volume balance and conductivity calibration. Compare tides and tributary inputs to test whether one average adequately describes the distribution. Reconstruct total salt from layer-volume-weighted salinity and check whether surface freshening reflects stratification rather than salt removal.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b224-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以鹽分混合與交換編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。採集表中底層鹽溫剖面，核對混合前後水量與導電度校正；對照潮相與支流入流，判斷單一平均值是否足以描述鹽分分布。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for salinity mixing and exchange, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Sample surface, middle and bottom salinity-temperature profiles and verify volume balance and conductivity calibration. Compare tides and tributary inputs to test whether one average adequately describes the distribution.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「鹽分混合與交換」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Salinity mixing and exchange\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","採集表中底層鹽溫剖面，核對混合前後水量與導電度校正；對照潮相與支流入流，判斷單一平均值是否足以描述鹽分分布。","浮門乾態自振週期可以直接當成水中的自振週期。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Sample surface, middle and bottom salinity-temperature profiles and verify volume balance and conductivity calibration.","A dry gate natural period can directly represent its wet natural period."],"answer":1,"explanation":"採集表中底層鹽溫剖面，核對混合前後水量與導電度校正；對照潮相與支流入流，判斷單一平均值是否足以描述鹽分分布。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Sample surface, middle and bottom salinity-temperature profiles and verify volume balance and conductivity calibration. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b224-v15-32","title":"鹽分混合與交換：失效診斷","titleEn":"Salinity mixing and exchange: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b224-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「鹽分混合與交換」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Salinity mixing and exchange” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"底層高鹽水可在表面變淡時仍滯留，造成密度分層並限制氧氣交換。把所有鹽度變化都歸因於門片動作，會漏掉河流、風和蒸發影響。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Saline bottom water can remain after surface freshening, maintaining stratification and limiting oxygen exchange. Attributing every salinity change to gate movement overlooks river, wind and evaporation effects. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：把所有鹽度變化都歸因於門片動作，會漏掉河流、風和蒸發影響。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Attributing every salinity change to gate movement overlooks river, wind and evaporation effects.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「平均鹽度降低就證明底層高鹽水已完全排出。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Lower mean salinity proves that all saline bottom water has been removed.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b224-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"底層高鹽水可在表面變淡時仍滯留，造成密度分層並限制氧氣交換。把所有鹽度變化都歸因於門片動作，會漏掉河流、風和蒸發影響。","textEn":"Saline bottom water can remain after surface freshening, maintaining stratification and limiting oxygen exchange. Attributing every salinity change to gate movement overlooks river, wind and evaporation effects.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b224-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「鹽分混合與交換」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Salinity mixing and exchange\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","壓力感測器讀數一致就證明共同取壓管沒有問題。","底層高鹽水可在表面變淡時仍滯留，造成密度分層並限制氧氣交換。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Matching pressure readings prove the shared impulse connection has no defect.","Saline bottom water can remain after surface freshening, maintaining stratification and limiting oxygen exchange."],"answer":2,"explanation":"底層高鹽水可在表面變淡時仍滯留，造成密度分層並限制氧氣交換。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Saline bottom water can remain after surface freshening, maintaining stratification and limiting oxygen exchange. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b224-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「壓力量測與不確定度」與「供氣網路可用度」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Pressure measurement uncertainty\" and \"Air-network availability\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b224-v15-33","title":"壓力量測與不確定度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Pressure measurement uncertainty: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b224-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「壓力量測與不確定度」如何影響威尼斯 MOSE 防潮系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Pressure measurement uncertainty” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Venice MOSE flood barriers”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"以壓力反推水深時，密度與感測誤差都進入結果。壓力計精度不是整體水位精度，導壓高程、氣泡和溫度也需要校核。 取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設壓力標準不確定度500 Pa、密度1025 kg/m³且暫視為精確，uh=up/(ρg)=0.04973 m；僅此誤差分量，非總誤差。 共同導壓管堵塞會讓多支感測器一致但錯誤，不能用數字吻合當獨立證據。若海水密度變動仍沿用淡水換算，也會產生持續水深偏差。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「壓力量測與不確定度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Inferring depth from pressure involves both density and sensor error. Transducer accuracy is not complete level accuracy because tapping elevation, trapped air and temperature also require checking. Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume pressure standard uncertainty 500 Pa and density 1025 kg/m³ treated as exact. uh=up/(ρg)=0.04973 m, representing this component only rather than total error. A shared blocked impulse line can make several sensors agree incorrectly. Agreement is not independence, and using freshwater density for changing seawater creates a persistent inferred-depth bias. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Pressure measurement uncertainty” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s².","failure":"常見誤解：「壓力感測器讀數一致就證明共同取壓管沒有問題。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Matching pressure readings prove the shared impulse connection has no defect.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「壓力量測與不確定度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Pressure measurement uncertainty”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b224-v15-33-k1","title":"壓力量測與不確定度","titleEn":"Pressure measurement uncertainty","text":"以壓力反推水深時，密度與感測誤差都進入結果。壓力計精度不是整體水位精度，導壓高程、氣泡和溫度也需要校核。","textEn":"Inferring depth from pressure involves both density and sensor error. Transducer accuracy is not complete level accuracy because tapping elevation, trapped air and temperature also require checking.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b224-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：壓力感測器讀數一致就證明共同取壓管沒有問題。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Matching pressure readings prove the shared impulse connection has no defect. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「壓力量測與不確定度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Pressure measurement uncertainty\" is correct?","options":["以壓力反推水深時，密度與感測誤差都進入結果。","壓力感測器讀數一致就證明共同取壓管沒有問題。","備援壓縮機能啟動就保證末端閥件取得足夠供氣。"],"optionsEn":["Inferring depth from pressure involves both density and sensor error.","Matching pressure readings prove the shared impulse connection has no defect.","A starting standby compressor guarantees sufficient air delivery at terminal valves."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以壓力反推水深時，密度與感測誤差都進入結果。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Inferring depth from pressure involves both density and sensor error. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b224-v15-34","title":"壓力量測與不確定度：定量估算","titleEn":"Pressure measurement uncertainty: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b224-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「壓力量測與不確定度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Pressure measurement uncertainty” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設壓力標準不確定度500 Pa、密度1025 kg/m³且暫視為精確，uh=up/(ρg)=0.04973 m；僅此誤差分量，非總誤差。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume pressure standard uncertainty 500 Pa and density 1025 kg/m³ treated as exact. uh=up/(ρg)=0.04973 m, representing this component only rather than total error. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以可追溯壓力基準校正量測鏈，檢查零點和跨度，再與獨立水位及溫鹽資料比較；把隨機不確定度和共同基準偏差分開列帳。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Calibrate the measurement chain with a traceable pressure reference, checking zero and span.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b224-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設壓力標準不確定度500 Pa、密度1025 kg/m³且暫視為精確，uh=up/(ρg)=0.04973 m；僅此誤差分量，非總誤差。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume pressure standard uncertainty 500 Pa and density 1025 kg/m³ treated as exact. uh=up/(ρg)=0.04973 m, representing this component only rather than total error.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b224-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「壓力量測與不確定度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Pressure measurement uncertainty\", which statement holds?","options":["氣體狀態換算可以直接用表壓取代絕對壓力。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。","只要有兩座鉸鏈，每座就永遠承受一半荷載。"],"optionsEn":["Gas-state calculations can directly substitute gauge pressure for absolute pressure.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s².","With two hinges each always carries exactly half the applied load."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b224-v15-35","title":"壓力量測與不確定度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Pressure measurement uncertainty: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b224-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「壓力量測與不確定度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Pressure measurement uncertainty” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以可追溯壓力基準校正量測鏈，檢查零點和跨度，再與獨立水位及溫鹽資料比較；把隨機不確定度和共同基準偏差分開列帳。另以密度不確定度傳播計算水深影響，對共同基準偏差採獨立外部測量核驗。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Calibrate the measurement chain with a traceable pressure reference, checking zero and span. Compare independent level and temperature-salinity data, separating random uncertainty from common datum bias. Propagate density uncertainty separately and use independent external measurements to test common reference bias in inferred depth. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以壓力量測與不確定度編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。以可追溯壓力基準校正量測鏈，檢查零點和跨度，再與獨立水位及溫鹽資料比較；把隨機不確定度和共同基準偏差分開列帳。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for pressure measurement uncertainty, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Calibrate the measurement chain with a traceable pressure reference, checking zero and span. Compare independent level and temperature-salinity data, separating random uncertainty from common datum bias.","failure":"注意干擾：共同導壓管堵塞會讓多支感測器一致但錯誤，不能用數字吻合當獨立證據。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A shared blocked impulse line can make several sensors agree incorrectly. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b224-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以可追溯壓力基準校正量測鏈，檢查零點和跨度，再與獨立水位及溫鹽資料比較；把隨機不確定度和共同基準偏差分開列帳。另以密度不確定度傳播計算水深影響，對共同基準偏差採獨立外部測量核驗。","textEn":"Calibrate the measurement chain with a traceable pressure reference, checking zero and span. Compare independent level and temperature-salinity data, separating random uncertainty from common datum bias. Propagate density uncertainty separately and use independent external measurements to test common reference bias in inferred depth.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b224-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以壓力量測與不確定度編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。以可追溯壓力基準校正量測鏈，檢查零點和跨度，再與獨立水位及溫鹽資料比較；把隨機不確定度和共同基準偏差分開列帳。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for pressure measurement uncertainty, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Calibrate the measurement chain with a traceable pressure reference, checking zero and span. Compare independent level and temperature-salinity data, separating random uncertainty from common datum bias.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「壓力量測與不確定度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Pressure measurement uncertainty\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","兩片門振幅相同就表示它們沒有相對運動。","以可追溯壓力基準校正量測鏈，檢查零點和跨度，再與獨立水位及溫鹽資料比較；把隨機不確定度和共同基準偏差分開列帳。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Two gates with equal amplitudes have no relative motion between them.","Calibrate the measurement chain with a traceable pressure reference, checking zero and span."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以可追溯壓力基準校正量測鏈，檢查零點和跨度，再與獨立水位及溫鹽資料比較；把隨機不確定度和共同基準偏差分開列帳。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Calibrate the measurement chain with a traceable pressure reference, checking zero and span. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b224-v15-36","title":"壓力量測與不確定度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Pressure measurement uncertainty: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b224-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「壓力量測與不確定度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Pressure measurement uncertainty” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"共同導壓管堵塞會讓多支感測器一致但錯誤，不能用數字吻合當獨立證據。若海水密度變動仍沿用淡水換算，也會產生持續水深偏差。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A shared blocked impulse line can make several sensors agree incorrectly. Agreement is not independence, and using freshwater density for changing seawater creates a persistent inferred-depth bias. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：若海水密度變動仍沿用淡水換算，也會產生持續水深偏差。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Agreement is not independence, and using freshwater density for changing seawater creates a persistent inferred-depth bias.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「壓力感測器讀數一致就證明共同取壓管沒有問題。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Matching pressure readings prove the shared impulse connection has no defect.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b224-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"共同導壓管堵塞會讓多支感測器一致但錯誤，不能用數字吻合當獨立證據。若海水密度變動仍沿用淡水換算，也會產生持續水深偏差。","textEn":"A shared blocked impulse line can make several sensors agree incorrectly. Agreement is not independence, and using freshwater density for changing seawater creates a persistent inferred-depth bias.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b224-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「壓力量測與不確定度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Pressure measurement uncertainty\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["共同導壓管堵塞會讓多支感測器一致但錯誤，不能用數字吻合當獨立證據。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","備援壓縮機能啟動就保證末端閥件取得足夠供氣。"],"optionsEn":["A shared blocked impulse line can make several sensors agree incorrectly.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A starting standby compressor guarantees sufficient air delivery at terminal valves."],"answer":0,"explanation":"共同導壓管堵塞會讓多支感測器一致但錯誤，不能用數字吻合當獨立證據。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A shared blocked impulse line can make several sensors agree incorrectly. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b224-v15-37","title":"供氣網路可用度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Air-network availability: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b224-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「供氣網路可用度」如何影響威尼斯 MOSE 防潮系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Air-network availability” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Venice MOSE flood barriers”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"供氣系統由壓縮、儲存、分配與閥件共同構成，備援壓縮機無法補償所有共用管路故障。可靠度必須先定義功能成功條件再計算。 假設兩台獨立壓縮機可用度各0.98、任一足夠，並串聯共同分配系統0.99；A=(1−0.02²)×0.99=0.989604，忽略修復動態。 共用閥卡住或管道淹水會使兩台壓縮機同時無法供氣，即使各自運轉正常。將設備啟動成功當作末端功能成功，會高估整體可用度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「供氣網路可用度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Air supply comprises compression, storage, distribution and valves. A spare compressor cannot compensate for every shared-pipe fault, so reliability calculations require a defined functional success condition. Assume two independent compressors each available 0.98, either sufficient, in series with distribution availability 0.99. A=(1−0.02²)×0.99=0.989604, excluding repair dynamics. A stuck shared valve or flooded pipe can defeat both running compressors. Equating successful equipment start with successful terminal delivery overstates availability of the complete functional supply chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Air-network availability” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設兩台獨立壓縮機可用度各0.98、任一足夠，並串聯共同分配系統0.99；A=(1−0.02²)×0.99=0.989604，忽略修復動態。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume two independent compressors each available 0.98, either sufficient, in series with distribution availability 0.99.","failure":"常見誤解：「備援壓縮機能啟動就保證末端閥件取得足夠供氣。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A starting standby compressor guarantees sufficient air delivery at terminal valves.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「供氣網路可用度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Air-network availability”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b224-v15-37-k1","title":"供氣網路可用度","titleEn":"Air-network availability","text":"供氣系統由壓縮、儲存、分配與閥件共同構成，備援壓縮機無法補償所有共用管路故障。可靠度必須先定義功能成功條件再計算。","textEn":"Air supply comprises compression, storage, distribution and valves. A spare compressor cannot compensate for every shared-pipe fault, so reliability calculations require a defined functional success condition.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b224-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：備援壓縮機能啟動就保證末端閥件取得足夠供氣。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A starting standby compressor guarantees sufficient air delivery at terminal valves. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「供氣網路可用度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Air-network availability\" is correct?","options":["備援壓縮機能啟動就保證末端閥件取得足夠供氣。","供氣系統由壓縮、儲存、分配與閥件共同構成，備援壓縮機無法補償所有共用管路故障。","總浮力大於自重就能直接決定翻板的唯一平衡角。"],"optionsEn":["A starting standby compressor guarantees sufficient air delivery at terminal valves.","Air supply comprises compression, storage, distribution and valves.","Buoyancy exceeding weight directly determines the unique flap equilibrium angle."],"answer":1,"explanation":"供氣系統由壓縮、儲存、分配與閥件共同構成，備援壓縮機無法補償所有共用管路故障。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Air supply comprises compression, storage, distribution and valves. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b224-v15-38","title":"供氣網路可用度：定量估算","titleEn":"Air-network availability: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b224-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「供氣網路可用度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Air-network availability” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設兩台獨立壓縮機可用度各0.98、任一足夠，並串聯共同分配系統0.99；A=(1−0.02²)×0.99=0.989604，忽略修復動態。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume two independent compressors each available 0.98, either sufficient, in series with distribution availability 0.99. A=(1−0.02²)×0.99=0.989604, excluding repair dynamics. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：從供氣需求追蹤至末端閥件，標出共用電源和管段，核對備機是否真能滿足所需流量；用歷史故障分類檢查獨立性假設。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Trace supply demand to terminal valves, marking common power and pipe sections.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b224-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設兩台獨立壓縮機可用度各0.98、任一足夠，並串聯共同分配系統0.99；A=(1−0.02²)×0.99=0.989604，忽略修復動態。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume two independent compressors each available 0.98, either sufficient, in series with distribution availability 0.99. A=(1−0.02²)×0.99=0.989604, excluding repair dynamics.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b224-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「供氣網路可用度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Air-network availability\", which statement holds?","options":["供氣量增加一定等比例增加浮門的排水體積。","浮門乾態自振週期可以直接當成水中的自振週期。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設兩台獨立壓縮機可用度各0.98、任一足夠，並串聯共同分配系統0.99。"],"optionsEn":["Increasing supplied air always proportionally increases the gates displaced water volume.","A dry gate natural period can directly represent its wet natural period.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume two independent compressors each available 0.98, either sufficient, in series with distribution availability 0.99."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設兩台獨立壓縮機可用度各0.98、任一足夠，並串聯共同分配系統0.99；A=(1−0.02²)×0.99=0.989604，忽略修復動態。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume two independent compressors each available 0.98, either sufficient, in series with distribution availability 0.99. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b224-v15-39","title":"供氣網路可用度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Air-network availability: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b224-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「供氣網路可用度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Air-network availability” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"從供氣需求追蹤至末端閥件，標出共用電源和管段，核對備機是否真能滿足所需流量；用歷史故障分類檢查獨立性假設。以末端壓力和流量證明功能交付，檢查共用分配管故障是否仍能使備機失去作用。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Trace supply demand to terminal valves, marking common power and pipe sections. Verify that a spare truly provides required flow and use historical failure categories to test independence assumptions. Demonstrate terminal pressure and flow delivery and test whether shared distribution faults still defeat the standby unit. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以供氣網路可用度編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。從供氣需求追蹤至末端閥件，標出共用電源和管段，核對備機是否真能滿足所需流量；用歷史故障分類檢查獨立性假設。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for air-network availability, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Trace supply demand to terminal valves, marking common power and pipe sections. Verify that a spare truly provides required flow and use historical failure categories to test independence assumptions.","failure":"注意干擾：共用閥卡住或管道淹水會使兩台壓縮機同時無法供氣，即使各自運轉正常。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A stuck shared valve or flooded pipe can defeat both running compressors. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b224-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"從供氣需求追蹤至末端閥件，標出共用電源和管段，核對備機是否真能滿足所需流量；用歷史故障分類檢查獨立性假設。以末端壓力和流量證明功能交付，檢查共用分配管故障是否仍能使備機失去作用。","textEn":"Trace supply demand to terminal valves, marking common power and pipe sections. Verify that a spare truly provides required flow and use historical failure categories to test independence assumptions. Demonstrate terminal pressure and flow delivery and test whether shared distribution faults still defeat the standby unit.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b224-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以供氣網路可用度編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。從供氣需求追蹤至末端閥件，標出共用電源和管段，核對備機是否真能滿足所需流量；用歷史故障分類檢查獨立性假設。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for air-network availability, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Trace supply demand to terminal valves, marking common power and pipe sections. Verify that a spare truly provides required flow and use historical failure categories to test independence assumptions.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「供氣網路可用度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Air-network availability\"?","options":["從供氣需求追蹤至末端閥件，標出共用電源和管段，核對備機是否真能滿足所需流量；用歷史故障分類檢查獨立性假設。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","海口關閉後，潟湖內水量就必定保持固定。"],"optionsEn":["Trace supply demand to terminal valves, marking common power and pipe sections.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Once the inlets close the lagoon water volume must remain constant."],"answer":0,"explanation":"從供氣需求追蹤至末端閥件，標出共用電源和管段，核對備機是否真能滿足所需流量；用歷史故障分類檢查獨立性假設。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Trace supply demand to terminal valves, marking common power and pipe sections. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b224-v15-40","title":"供氣網路可用度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Air-network availability: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"prerequisiteIds":["b224-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「供氣網路可用度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Air-network availability” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"共用閥卡住或管道淹水會使兩台壓縮機同時無法供氣，即使各自運轉正常。將設備啟動成功當作末端功能成功，會高估整體可用度。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A stuck shared valve or flooded pipe can defeat both running compressors. Equating successful equipment start with successful terminal delivery overstates availability of the complete functional supply chain. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：將設備啟動成功當作末端功能成功，會高估整體可用度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Equating successful equipment start with successful terminal delivery overstates availability of the complete functional supply chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「備援壓縮機能啟動就保證末端閥件取得足夠供氣。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A starting standby compressor guarantees sufficient air delivery at terminal valves.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b224-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"共用閥卡住或管道淹水會使兩台壓縮機同時無法供氣，即使各自運轉正常。將設備啟動成功當作末端功能成功，會高估整體可用度。","textEn":"A stuck shared valve or flooded pipe can defeat both running compressors. Equating successful equipment start with successful terminal delivery overstates availability of the complete functional supply chain.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]},{"id":"b224-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「供氣網路可用度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Air-network availability\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","共用閥卡住或管道淹水會使兩台壓縮機同時無法供氣，即使各自運轉正常。","總浮力大於自重就能直接決定翻板的唯一平衡角。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","A stuck shared valve or flooded pipe can defeat both running compressors.","Buoyancy exceeding weight directly determines the unique flap equilibrium angle."],"answer":1,"explanation":"共用閥卡住或管道淹水會使兩台壓縮機同時無法供氣，即使各自運轉正常。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A stuck shared valve or flooded pipe can defeat both running compressors. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-mose-test","v15s-venice-first","v15s-abb-mose","v15s-usace-steel","v15s-usace-mechanical"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
